VisTouch anomaly screen & repair log (session-level, applied during the
non-overlapping segmentation rebuild)

Rule (tactile, per 100 Hz session series):
  repair a point only if |residual vs 5-tap median| > 0.5 x file dynamic
  range AND > 50 raw units  ->  replaced by local median value

Rule (audio, per 16 kHz session waveform):
  repair a sample only if |residual vs 5-tap median| > 15 robust sigma
  AND |x| > 10 x file RMS AND |x| > 0.25 full scale  ->  linear interp

Result over all 24 sessions:
  tactile points repaired : 67
  audio samples repaired  : 2
  video frames modified   : 0

Everything else in the released files is a faithful cut of the raw sensor
recordings (audio sliced at 16 kHz sample boundaries, tactile resampled to
a uniform 100 Hz grid from the raw integer-second stream, video copied
frame-exact at 30 fps). Segments are strictly non-overlapping and tile the
valid tri-modal intersection of each session.
